    "knowledge": "1. Source Files & RTL Logic Analyzed:\n   - `src/lsu/lsu.sv`:\n     - Line 261: `mmu #(.P(P), .TLB_ENTRIES(P.DTLB_ENTRIES), .IMMU(0)) dtlb(.clk, .reset, ..., .Size(LSUFunct3M[1:0]));`. `LSUFunct3M` is 3 bits, but `.Size` only passes the bottom 2 bits (`LSUFunct3M[1:0]`). For `amocas.q` (`Funct3 == 3'b100`), `Size[1:0]` evaluates to `2'b00`.\n     - Line 428-432: `CASMatchM` correctly compares 128 bits for `amocas.q` (`default: CASMatchM = ReadDataM[P.XLEN*2-1:0] == ComparePairM;`).\n     - Line 452: `swbytemask` takes `LSUFunct3M` (3 bits) and computes a 16-byte mask (`(2**(2**4) - 1)`).\n   - `src/mmu/mmu.sv`:\n     - Lines 35, 139-144: `Size` port is declared as `input logic [1:0] Size;`. `case (Size)` only defines `2'b00` (byte: `DataMisalignedM = 0`), `2'b01` (halfword: `VAdr[0]`), `2'b10` (word: `VAdr[1]|VAdr[0]`), and `2'b11` (doubleword: `|VAdr[2:0]`).\n     - Truncated `amocas.q` falls into `2'b00`, making `DataMisalignedM = 1'b0`. Neither `LoadMisalignedFaultM`, `StoreAmoMisalignedFaultM`, nor `MisalignedCausesAccessFaultM` is asserted.\n   - `src/ieu/controller.sv`:\n     - Line 353: `assign SFenceVmaD = PrivilegedD & (InstrD[31:25] == 7'b0001001);` only decodes `sfence.vma`, omitting Svinval instructions (`sinval.vma` `7'b0001011`, `sfence.w.inval` and `sfence.inval.ir` `7'b0001100`).\n   - `src/privileged/csrs.sv` & `src/privileged/csr.sv`:\n     - Lines 285-288: `STCE` is defined as `P.SSTC_SUPPORTED & (PrivilegeModeW == P.M_MODE | (MCOUNTEREN_REGW[1] & ENVCFG_STCE));`. `mcounteren.TM` (bit 1) erroneously gates `stimecmp` read and write permissions in S-mode.\n     - Spike caveat: The installed Spike binary segfaults (SIGSEGV, exit code 139) whenever `stimecmp` is accessed with `--isa=rv64gc_sstc`. Spike CANNOT be used as an oracle for `sstc`.\n   - `src/mmu/tlb/tlbramline.sv`:\n     - Lines 40-55: Verified that `ptereg[54]` stores `|d[60:54]` and reconstructs `line[60]`, proving leaf PTE reserved bits [60:54] are properly compacted into bit 60.\n   - `src/fpu/postproc/round.sv`:\n     - Lines 124, 196-198: Analyzed `NormSticky` and `FpRound` for `Bf16Dst`. Boolean algebra proves `Round | Sticky` evaluates identically whether bit -2 is in `NormSticky` or not.\n   - `src/ieu/bmu/cnt.sv` & `bmuctrl.sv`:\n     - Verified `lzcmux64` operand packing for `clzw` and `ctzw`.\n\n2. Specification References:\n   - RISC-V Atomic Compare-and-Swap (Zacas) Extension Specification (Version 1.0):\n     - Section 2 ('Word/Doubleword/Quadword CAS (AMOCAS.W/D/Q)'): 'The register-pair form of AMOCAS is AMOCAS.D in RV32 and AMOCAS.Q in RV64... AMOCAS.Q operates on a 128-bit quadword. AMOCAS.Q requires natural alignment: the address must be 16-byte aligned. If the effective address is not naturally aligned, an address-misaligned exception or an access-fault exception shall be raised.'\n   - RISC-V Instruction Set Manual, Volume I: Unprivileged Architecture:\n     - Chapter 8 ('A Extension'): 'An address-misaligned exception or access-fault exception is generated if the address is not naturally aligned to the size of the operand.'\n   - Local `isa_docs` disclosure: Local ISA documentation was unavailable in the worktree (`\"isa_docs\": \"\"`). Normative rules were verified directly against official RISC-V specifications and cross-checked against Spike reference behavior.\n\n3. Toolchain & Simulation Environment Insights:\n   - Compiler: `/home/rafay/riscv/bin/riscv64-unknown-elf-gcc` (GCC 15.2.0).\n   - Spike: `/home/rafay/riscv/bin/spike` (Spike 1.1.1-dev). Supports `--isa=rv64gc_zacas`. Unaligned `amocas.q` correctly causes Spike to trap.\n   - Verilator Simulator: `sim/verilator/wkdir/rv64gc_testbench/Vtestbench` is pre-built and supports Zacas.\n   - Trap vectors: Trap handlers must be 4-byte aligned (`.align 4` or `.align 2`) because `mtvec` bits [1:0] are forced to 0 in Direct mode.\n   - Testbench completion protocol: Verilator `testbench.sv` triggers `$finish` on `32'h0000006f` (`1: j 1b`). A failure handler sh