      "fixer": {
        "changed": true,
        "report": "ROOT CAUSE: In src/lsu/lsu.sv line 261, the memory operation size is passed to the MMU as .Size(LSUFunct3M[1:0]), truncating the 3-bit funct3 field to 2 bits. For amocas.q (quadword, 128-bit), LSUFunct3M = 3'b100, which truncates to 2'b00 (byte). In src/mmu/mmu.sv, the Size input port is only 2 bits wide and the misalignment case statement only handles byte/half/word/double (2'b00 through 2'b11), with no provision for quadword. Since the truncated Size is 2'b00, DataMisalignedM is always 0 for amocas.q, regardless of address alignment. This means the core never raises an address-misaligned exception for unaligned amocas.q, violating RISC-V Zacas Specification Section 2 which mandates 16-byte natural alignment.\n\nMINIMAL FIX (3 files, 6 line changes):\n1. src/mmu/mmu.sv: (a) Widen Size port from [1:0] to [2:0]; (b) Truncate to Size[1:0] when passing to pmachecker and pmpchecker (preserving their 2-bit interface); (c) Add case 3'b100: DataMisalignedM = |VAdr[3:0]; to the misalignment check.\n2. src/lsu/lsu.sv: Change .Size(LSUFunct3M[1:0]) to .Size(LSUFunct3M) to pass the full 3-bit size.\n3. src/ifu/ifu.sv: Change .Size(2'b10) to .Size(3'b010) in the IMMU instantiation for consistency.\n\nFILES MODIFIED:\n- src/mmu/mmu.sv (4 changes: port width, 2 downstream truncations, case statement)\n- src/lsu/lsu.sv (1 change: Size connection)\n- src/ifu/ifu.sv (1 change: Size literal)\n\nTARGETED TEST OUTCOME: The reproducer script was executed against the patched DUT. Before the fix, the reproducer exited with code 1 (mismatch confirmed \u2014 DUT failed to trap on unaligned amocas.q with offset 8, triggering Watch Dog Time Out). After the fix, the DUT correctly traps on the unaligned amocas.q, the trap handler writes 1 to tohost, and the test completes successfully. The reproducer exits with code 0 (DUT behaves correctly). The positive control test (aligned amocas.q at offset 0) also passes on both Spike and DUT. The fix is defensible, minimal, and does not weaken any checks."
